  {
   "id": "zHJkroSOAgAJ",
   "from": "Julio Torres",
   "author": "e511f911cbbb2bd0",
   "date": "2021-06-24T15:56:05Z",
   "subject": "Question about subsetting datasets after importing to geomorph",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">Hi folks, <br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">I am trying to assess allometry in my dataset using procD.lm ( )  and using Sex, Sites and Species as factors.</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"> My problem I think is about data manipulations with arrays and lists within geomorph. <br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">I have several NAs in the variable Sex and can not include this model because I have 3 factors (female, males and NA) instead of two (female, male).<br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">I will really appreciate it if someone can help me with the code to subset my dataset, filtering specimens and data associated with these NA. <br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">Below my code<br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"># import datasets<br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">dorsal &lt;- readland.tps(&quot;./data/dorsal.tps&quot;, specID = &quot;imageID&quot;)</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">classifier_dor &lt;- read.csv(file = &quot;./data/dor_classifier.csv&quot;, header = TRUE, na.strings = c(&quot;NA&quot;,&quot;&quot;))</div><div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\" class=\"gmail_default\"># run gpa analysis<br></div></div><div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\" class=\"gmail_default\">gpa_dorsal &lt;- gpagen(dorsal, curves= NULL)</div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\" class=\"gmail_default\"># create a geomorph.data.frame<br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\" class=\"gmail_default\">gdf_dorsal &lt;- geomorph.data.frame(gpa_dorsal, Sex= classifier_dor$sexo, Sites = classifier_dor$sites,<br>                                  Species= classifier_dor$species) <br></div></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\" class=\"gmail_default\">Thanks in advance</div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\" class=\"gmail_default\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\" class=\"gmail_default\">Julio</div><br></div><div><br></div>-- <br><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Becario Posdoctoral CONICET</b><br><i>Laboratorio de Genética Evolutiva, Instituto de Biología Subtropical (CONICET-UNaM), Facultad de Ciencias Exactas Químicas y Naturales, Universidad Nacional de Misiones, Félix de Azara 1552, CP N3300LQF Posadas, Argentina.<br></i><b>Investigador asociado</b><br><i>Instituto de Investigación Biológica el Paraguay (IIBP),<br></i><div><i>Del Escudo 1607 casi avenida Brasilia, CP1425, Asunción, Paraguay<span style=\"font-size:12.7272720336914px;line-height:25.6000003814697px;text-align:center\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"verdana, sans-serif\"><br></font></span></span></i></div><div><i><span style=\"font-size:12.7272720336914px;line-height:25.6000003814697px;text-align:center\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"verdana, sans-serif\"><a href=\"https://cv.conacyt.gov.py/publicar/cv?id=9fc5d2b9dd593dd7fffa921bc589f7e2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cv.conacyt.gov.py/publicar/cv?id%3D9fc5d2b9dd593dd7fffa921bc589f7e2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484095380000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3CvcdzVI5e2N72w43MG6Up\">CV_Py</a></font></span></span></i></div><div><i><span style=\"font-size:12.7272720336914px;line-height:25.6000003814697px;text-align:center\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"></span></span></i></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><span style=\"font-size:12.7272720336914px;line-height:25.6000003814697px;text-align:center\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"verdana, sans-serif\"><a href=\"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Julio-Torres\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Julio-Torres&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484095380000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ItVkSb2VDoB__o2OooLu4\">Researchgate</a><br></font></span></span></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><span style=\"font-size:12.7272720336914px;line-height:25.6000003814697px;text-align:center\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"verdana, sans-serif\"><a href=\"http://linkedin.com/in/julio-torres-a27a2351\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://linkedin.com/in/julio-torres-a27a2351&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484095380000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1F_aItmKMxXQ0MftQw-vM-\">Linkedin</a><br></font></span></span></div></div></div></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
