   "subject": "RE: [geomorph-r-package] Question about subsetting datasets after importing to geomorph",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">If the classifiers and specimens are in the same order, you can simply identify which elements are NA, and remove them from both components of the dataset.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Pseudo-code example:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Missing &lt;- which(<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484095383000&amp;usg=AOvVaw13zkAJran-B5LZ-iJ3duNP\">is.na</a>(x))<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Complete &lt;- Mydata[-Missing]<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Complete.shapes &lt;-myshapes[,,-Missing]<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Dean<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\">Dr. Dean C. Adams<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\">Director of Graduate Education, EEB Program<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\">Professor<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\">Department of Ecology, Evolution, and Organismal Biology<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\">Iowa State University<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><a href=\"https://faculty.sites.iastate.edu/dcadams/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://faculty.sites.iastate.edu/dcadams/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484095383000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1XOz6sCaY_0JYdPGQIkfwP\"><span style=\"color:#0563c1\">https://faculty.sites.iastate.edu/dcadams/</span></a><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\">phone: <a href=\"tel:(515)%20294-3834\" value=\"+15152943834\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">515-294-3834</a><u></u><u></u></span></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b>From:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;\r\n<b>On Behalf Of </b>Julio Torres<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Thursday, June 24, 2021 10:56 AM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [geomorph-r-package] Question about subsetting datasets after importing to geomorph<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Hi folks,\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">I am trying to assess allometry in my dataset using procD.lm ( )  and using Sex, Sites and Species as factors.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">My problem I think is about data manipulations with arrays and lists within geomorph.\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">I have several NAs in the variable Sex and can not include this model because I have 3 factors (female, males and NA) instead of two (female, male).<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">I will really appreciate it if someone can help me with the code to subset my dataset, filtering specimens and data associated with these NA.\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Below my code<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"># import datasets<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">dorsal &lt;- readland.tps(&quot;./data/dorsal.tps&quot;, specID = &quot;imageID&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">classifier_dor &lt;- read.csv(file = &quot;./data/dor_classifier.csv&quot;, header = TRUE, na.strings = c(&quot;NA&quot;,&quot;&quot;))<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"># run gpa analysis<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">gpa_dorsal &lt;- gpagen(dorsal, curves= NULL)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"># create a geomorph.data.frame<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">gdf_dorsal &lt;- geomorph.data.frame(gpa_dorsal, Sex= classifier_dor$sexo, Sites = classifier_dor$sites,<br>\r\n                                  Species= classifier_dor$species) <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Thanks in advance<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Julio<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">-- <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b>Becario Posdoctoral CONICET</b><br>\r\n<i>Laboratorio de Genética Evolutiva, Instituto de Biología Subtropical (CONICET-UNaM), Facultad de Ciencias Exactas Químicas y Naturales, Universidad Nacional de Misiones, Félix de Azara 1552, CP N3300LQF Posadas, Argentina.<br>\r\n</i><b>Investigador asociado</b><br>\r\n<i>Instituto de Investigación Biológica el Paraguay (IIBP),</i><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><i>Del Escudo 1607 casi avenida Brasilia, CP1425, Asunción, Paraguay</i><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><a href=\"https://cv.conacyt.gov.py/publicar/cv?id=9fc5d2b9dd593dd7fffa921bc589f7e2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cv.conacyt.gov.py/publicar/cv?id%3D9fc5d2b9dd593dd7fffa921bc589f7e2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484095383000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3d68FN3TCeXeRjc6LMsB8O\"><i><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif\">CV_Py</span></i></a><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><a href=\"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Julio-Torres\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Julio-Torres&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484095383000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0_6AkSOD7NGCRasNg3WFwm\"><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif\">Researchgate</span></a><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><a href=\"http://linkedin.com/in/julio-torres-a27a2351\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://linkedin.com/in/julio-torres-a27a2351&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484095383000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1wfRiWKu-UNM41o8jSTe91\"><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif\">Linkedin</span></a><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></div>"
